WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.467
The three access paths are easier to remember when you follow where the model weights go.

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:11.082
For a public local model, you download the weights and run them on your hardware.

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:19.642
For a gated Hugging Face model, you first request access, authenticate with a Hugging Face token, download the weights,

00:00:19.642 --> 00:00:22.052
and then still run locally.

00:00:22.052 --> 00:00:29.122
For a hosted A P I, the weights stay with the provider and your application sends requests to the provider's

00:00:29.122 --> 00:00:30.880
infrastructure.

00:00:31.747 --> 00:00:38.733
Ask one question whenever the terminology becomes confusing: where are the model weights actually running?
